            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-befe6510142e-0003-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case concerns whether the federal government can terminate a reservation held in trust for the White Mountain Apache Tribe."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "befe6510142eccd3b6e161301b2ae20ff2572538e610d9cd6d474169569f34c9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-befe6510142e-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States argues that the trust over Fort Apache lands restrains alienation of the property and immunizes it from state taxation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "befe6510142eccd3b6e161301b2ae20ff2572538e610d9cd6d474169569f34c9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-befe6510142e-0003-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Only Congress has the power to terminate the reservation; the executive branch cannot terminate it."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "United States",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "befe6510142eccd3b6e161301b2ae20ff2572538e610d9cd6d474169569f34c9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-befe6510142e-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States, the vast majority of the buildings and historic district area of Fort Apache are used today for school and administrative purposes."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "United States",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "befe6510142eccd3b6e161301b2ae20ff2572538e610d9cd6d474169569f34c9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-befe6510142e-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States, when Congress places land in trust for Indians, it restrains alienation of the property and immunizes the property from State taxation."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "United States (Petitioner)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent (Robert C. Brauchli)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "befe6510142eccd3b6e161301b2ae20ff2572538e610d9cd6d474169569f34c9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-befe6510142e-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 33,
                "start": 32
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent (Robert C. Brauchli), the Secretary of the Interior voluntarily took control of the buildings, distinguishing the trust from a bare trust."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "befe6510142eccd3b6e161301b2ae20ff2572538e610d9cd6d474169569f34c9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-befe6510142e-0003-0001",
                "ev-befe6510142e-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 57,
                "start": 56
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Government, the government's liability ends when it relinquishes control of the buildings and the Tribe assumes responsibility for them."
        }
      ],
